  "description": "Step drop-off across the guided first three levels (SPEC §14).\n\nPer-step rather than per-level because tutorial drop-off is where a casual puzzle game bleeds installs, and 'they quit' is not an actionable finding — 'they quit on the step that asks for a double tap' is.\n\n**`step` is the enum name, never an index.** The curriculum will be reordered, and a funnel keyed on position would silently start comparing two different lessons.\n\n**There is no `tutorial.skipped` event**, though SPEC §14 names one. A skip is `tutorial.completed` with `skipped=true` and a `last_step`, because both endings write `AppData.hasCompletedTutorial` and both are the end of the tutorial. Two events for one transition would mean every funnel had to remember to union them.\n\n**Replaying from Settings re-arms the run**, so a small number of repeat `tutorial.completed` events per install is expected rather than a bug. Rates against a distinct-install denominator read slightly high because of it.\n\n**Loki-backed, so nothing here can see past Grafana Cloud's log retention.** Widening the time picker does not widen the answer.\n\n**Delivery is at-least-once.** A record can rarely ship twice (export acknowledged, process died before the buffer delete), so read raw counts as approximate. Panels that count *installs* rather than records are immune to it by construction — a duplicate lands in the same `install_id` series and collapses.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
